      "content": "I hear the desperate and rational plea to stop bleeding pain, and it is entirely understandable to consider giving up when the cost feels too high. You are right that \"just trying again\" can feel like getting hurt over and over, but ending it all is not the same as \"exiting a bad life to start a new one.\"\nStop thinking of \"restarting\" as a financial venture where you hope to earn your life back; instead, try to stop treating your 22 years as a \"sunk cost\" and accept that you only get to count the \"unspent\" years so you can stop the self-hatred.\nPlease consider talking to a therapist or a crisis support line who can help you navigate this feeling of hopelessness without having to \"go it alone\" in the darkness.\nIf you feel unsafe because of these suicidal thoughts, please call 988 (in the US and many Canadian and some other countries) or 111 (in the UK and many other countries) for immediate support.\nI hope you can take a small \"one\" step to get help and find someone in the \"real world\" just for the \"one\" \"real\" \"moment\" to \"re",
